+## Choosing rate and burst
+
+`rate` is the sustained number of requests per second a client may make and
+`burst` is how many it can make at once after being idle. A good starting
+point is a burst of about two seconds of traffic: `New(5, 10)`.
+
+## Behind a reverse proxy
+
+`ClientIP` uses the address of the TCP connection. Behind a load balancer that
+is the balancer's address, so every client shares one bucket. Write a
+`KeyFunc` that reads the header your proxy sets, and only trust it when the
+connection comes from the proxy; otherwise clients can pick their own key.
+
+## Memory
+
+Each key keeps a small bucket. Call `Forget` periodically (for example every
+minute with `Forget(10 * time.Minute)`) to drop idle ones.
+
+## Development
+
 Run `go test ./...` before sending a change.
